@page
@model Cs313Model
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "CS 313";
}
<header class="page-header">
    <p class="page-kicker">
        <i class="bi bi-mortarboard" aria-hidden="true"></i> Coursework case study
    </p>
    <h1>
        @ViewData["Title"]
    </h1>
    @if (ViewData["Message"] is string pageMessage && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(pageMessage))
    {
        <p class="page-intro">
            @pageMessage
        </p>
    }
</header>
<div class="reading-layout">
    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Coursework sections">
        <p class="page-kicker">
            On this page
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="#php-project">CS 313 PHP Project 2017</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#java-project">CS 313 Java</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#team-project">CS 313 Team Project</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <a asp-page="/College/Index">Back to coursework</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="reading-main">
        <section class="content-panel prose" id="php-project">
            <h2>
                CS 313 PHP Project 2017
            </h2>
            <p>
                This class project work highlights class assignment work utilizing the PHP programming language. I was able to learn and gain a foundational understanding
                of the PHP programming lanague and how to use it with various databases. The primary database engine that I used was PostgreSQL.
                This project included the use of Bootstrap, jQuery, PostgreSQL and other optional libraries.
            </p>
            @*
            <p>
                <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://evening-dawn-85312.herokuapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CS 313 PHP Site >></a>
            </p>
        *@
        </section>
        <section class="content-panel prose" id="java-project">
            <h2>
                CS 313 Java
            </h2>
            <p>
                This second class project space was utilizing the Java programming language. I implemented standard Java Server Pages and various servlets to accomplish
                class assignments. I used the Netbeans IDE and maven for building the Java applications.
                This project included the use of Maven, Bootstrap, jQuery, and database technologies.
            </p>
            @*
            <p>
                <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://hidden-plateau-66868.herokuapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CS 313 Java Site >></a>
            </p>
        *@
        </section>
        <section class="content-panel prose" id="team-project">
            <h2>
                CS 313 Team Project
            </h2>
            <p>
                This is an example of our CS 313 Team project written in Java.
                This project included the use of Google APIs, Bootstrap, jQuery, and other optional libraries.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://github.com/MCLifeLeader/cs313php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub CS 313 PHP >></a>
                @* <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://evening-dawn-85312.herokuapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Heroku Hosted Site >></a> *@
                <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://github.com/MCLifeLeader/cs313java" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub CS 313 Java >></a>
                @* <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://hidden-plateau-66868.herokuapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Heroku Hosted Site >></a> *@
                <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://github.com/MCLifeLeader/CS313Team" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub CS 313 Team Project >></a>
                @* <a class="btn btn-info btn-site" href="https://cs313team.herokuapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CS 313 Team Project >></a> *@
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="reading-aside">
